# What must NOT be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# vercel.json sets outputDirectory: "frontend", so every byte under frontend/ is
# uploaded and served. After the 22 Aug character upload that came to 983MB, of
# which 736MB was frontend/assets/models3d/_incoming — the raw .gltf + .bin + png
# a supplier ships, which the ingest already packed losslessly into the .glb files
# under packs/. No player ever fetches a byte of it.
#
# That is not merely waste. A deploy that large is slow at best and refused at
# worst, and a refused deploy means the model library silently does not reach the
# site: every game the forge builds 404s on its characters and the creator is
# charged for a build that cannot run. The uploads must stay in git — they are the
# source a re-ingest runs from, and re-downloading them is not possible from the
# build environment — so ignoring them here is the fix, not deleting them.
frontend/assets/models3d/_incoming/
frontend/assets/sprites/_incoming/

# Dev-only. The test suite compiles api/ and shared/ into its own throwaway tree;
# neither the tests nor the asset tooling is part of the deployed app.
tests/
tools/
.testbuild/
